68
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:37,240
For set associative caches, if there are n ways, then we have n possible candidates

69
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,960
for replacement.

70
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:45,080
In an ideal world, we would use belated optimal replacement policy where we would evict the

71
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:50,360
block that would be used furthest away in the future.

72
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:54,280
This maximizes our ability to reuse blocks in the cache effectively.

73
00:05:54,280 --> 00:06:00,960
However, this policy requires perfect knowledge of the future and is impossible to achieve.

74
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:05,840
More practical common policies include FIFO, which evicts the oldest block by tracking

75
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,280
