97
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:50,640
After this, way 1 becomes the least recently used in the set.

98
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:53,360
The next access is to address 2B.

99
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:57,840
This byte is within the same block as 2A, so we have a cache hit, and nothing changes

100
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:00,900
